This package contains the public protocol contracts for the Entra.EventHandlers ecosystem.

It is fully MIT-licensed, dependency-free, and safe to use in open-source,
commercial, and proprietary applications.

Contents include:

- Event models
- Response models
- Action models
- Handler interfaces
- Protocol constants
- Shared primitives

The abstractions package intentionally does not include:

- Fluent response builders
- Handler base classes
- Hosting integrations
- Validation pipelines
- Logging
- Dependency injection

Additional packages extend these abstractions with implementation, hosting,
and security capabilities:

- Entra.EventHandlers — External ID implementation layer (BSL)
- Entra.EventHandlers.Workforce — Workforce implementation layer (BSL)
- Entra.EventHandlers.AspNetCore — ASP.NET Core hosting adapter (BSL)
- Entra.EventHandlers.AzureFunctions — Azure Functions hosting adapter (BSL)
- Entra.EventHandlers.Security — PasswordSubmit decryption and Azure Key Vault integration (BSL)

These packages provide strongly typed handlers, fluent response builders,
security integrations, hosting infrastructure, routing, dependency injection
integration, and request/response adapters built on top of the abstractions.
